## 🧪 TESTING STANDARDS

### Estructura de Tests

```
test/
├── core/
│   ├── error/
│   ├── result/
│   └── logging/
├── features/
│   └── gossip/
│       ├── data/
│       │   ├── datasources/
│       │   ├── models/
│       │   └── repositories/
│       ├── domain/
│       │   ├── entities/
│       │   └── usecases/
│       └── presentation/
│           └── controllers/
└── widget_test.dart
```

### Testing Patterns

**Unit Tests:**
```dart
void main() {
  group('GossipRepository', () {
    late GossipRepositoryImpl repository;
    late MockRemoteDataSource mockRemote;
    late MockLocalDataSource mockLocal;

    setUp(() {
      mockRemote = MockRemoteDataSource();
      mockLocal = MockLocalDataSource();
      repository = GossipRepositoryImpl(
        remoteDataSource: mockRemote,
        localDataSource: mockLocal,
      );
    });

    test('debe retornar gossips del remoto', () async {
      // Arrange
      when(mockRemote.getGossips(any))
        .thenAnswer((_) async => [mockModel]);

      // Act
      final result = await repository.getGossips(query);

      // Assert
      expect(result.isSuccess, isTrue);
      expect(result.successValue!.length, 1);
    });
  });
}
```

**Mocks con Mockito:**
```dart
@GenerateMocks([
  GossipRemoteDataSource,
  GossipLocalDataSource,
])
void main() {
  // Tests aquí
}

// Genera: gossip_repository_impl_test.mocks.dart
```

**Comando:**
```bash
flutter pub run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs
```

### Coverage

**Objetivo:** >80% de coverage en domain y data layers

```bash
# Ejecutar tests con coverage
flutter test --coverage

# Ver reporte (requiere lcov)
genhtml coverage/lcov.info -o coverage/html
open coverage/html/index.html
```

